A||||9||GodSend||Blocking off egr tube?||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||05-08-2001||12:25 PM||||  I am sure I remember seeing posts from several members regarding fixing an EGR tube leak by blocking the holes?<P>  Well one of the flanges around the end that meets the egr has totally cracked and fallen off.  <P>  What is the easiest way to block off these holes? (do I do it on both ends?)  Thanks guys. (this will be a temp fix untill I can track downa new tube that wont cost me 130 bucks Canadian from the dealer !  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||05-08-2001||12:38 PM||||I've seen folks just clamp the ends of the tubes flat.<BR>If yours is broken at the EGR valve end, just flatten the end of the tube that goes up to the plenum, and unplug and block the vacuum hose at the EGR valve. <BR>Try looking in the boneyards for EGR tubes from 2.8 Firebirds. They'll fit, but you have to slot the holes in the flange. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||GodSend||05-08-2001||03:47 PM||||I grabbed a tube from a 2.8 camero from the bone yard..I slotted the one end fine, but the tube itself was too long.  I tried to bend it but could not come up with the shape that would fit<P>the flanges from the camero version were not free like the ones on the fiero (ie they were stuck in the wrong possition).. i could not turn them, and therefore the holes in flanges were way off!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by GodSend (edited 05-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||05-08-2001||05:16 PM||||Oh. Oops.<BR>You are the first person that I've heard have a problem with an F-body EGR tube. <BR>I will stop telling people that they work. <BR>Can't believe everything you read. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||11
Z||000004||GT GT 87||05-08-2001||05:44 PM||||I have the 2.8 , where it meets the manifold , loosen the flange bolts enough to slide a piece of tin can , cut to fit,  long is good , easier to slide under, then tighten the bolts. At the egr end , loosen the egr , and where it meets the Y-pipe,  slide another piece in ............   I have tried beer can metal " since I have so many laying around " but I think they are to thin...........  Good luck       STEVE<P>[This message has been edited by GT GT 87 (edited 05-08-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by GT GT 87 (edited 05-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||GodSend||05-08-2001||09:12 PM||||Thats exactly what I did last weekend.  It seemed to work like a charm for a few days, but now I get a weird surge from the engine I never had before.<P>  When I am driving along at a constant speed I can feel the engine loose power (ever so slightly .. its not a big loss), as soon as I give her even a little more gas it picks right back up, but you can feel the hesitation for a slight second.<P>  I am thinking this has something to do with my crappy 'can method' fix.  Im going to need to car to get emission tested in the fall anyways, so I am going to have to replace the egr tube anyways... arent i?||||reg||6
Z||000006||lou_dias||05-09-2001||12:37 AM||||I noticed a big gain in power from 3000rpm on...  I blocked it off at both ends of where the tube would go...  The valve is cracked where it meets the crossover and I left the vacuum tube on.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||05-09-2001||07:17 AM||||chevy S10 2.8 is what I put on mine. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fiero-Tex||05-09-2001||01:29 PM||||(this will be a temp fix untill I can track downa new tube that wont cost me 130 bucks Canadian from the dealer !   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>[/B][/QUOTE]If you can find out the part number for the tube and GM still has some in stock you might be in luck.  I have found several parts for 1/2 the price of the dealer at (gmpartsdirect.com). You have to search by part number for Fiero parts, but you get a new part at half the dealer price.<P>Good Luck!<P><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
